{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115966",
      "title": "Understanding How Pipes Are Executed",
      "lectureOrder": 172,
      "videoOrder": 164,
      "sourceHash": "4903c3ba1d5c6ad5b674762ff7a02ddee3f16542592bc1891ab8b610c7a00f77",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.761,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "[Maximilian So why can't we click these items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 5.463,
          "en": "when using the SortPipe?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.36,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "Well, we can click them, I can tell you that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "onReset is getting triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "and the code in there will execute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 18.11,
          "en": "but Angular will not update this part of the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "it will not re-execute this SortPipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "on the updated historicTemperatures array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 28.5,
          "en": "and therefore we still see the old list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.5,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "So Angular is reusing the old result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 35.793,
          "en": "of this SortPipe transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "And this is no bug, but instead an intended feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 45.32,
          "en": "because the idea is that those pipe transform methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.36,
          "end": 48.93,
          "en": "can potentially be executed quite a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.93,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "After all, you are using them in your templates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "and therefore, whenever the template is rendered again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "because anything changed anywhere in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 61.893,
          "en": "all those pipe transform methods would be triggered again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.88,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "So those transform methods can potentially run a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "And by default, Angular prevents that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 75.32,
          "en": "by caching the return value and by only rerunning transform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "if the input value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 83.37,
          "en": "Now, you could say, yeah, but the input value does change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.37,
          "end": 85.38,
          "en": "if I click one of these numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.38,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "after all, it will be replaced with the number 18.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 91.23,
          "en": "And you would be right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "but since we're dealing with an array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "and I'm overwriting a value inside of that array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 99.81,
          "en": "instead of the entire array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.81,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "Angular will ignore that change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "because Angular will check for changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "by comparing the new value with the old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "And in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "arrays and objects when changed internally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "as a whole, don't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "Arrays and objects in JavaScript are in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "reference values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "which mean the input value we get is just a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "to the array or object in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "And attached to this lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "you'll find a link to an article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "which explores this concept in greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 135.723,
          "en": "in case it's brand new to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "But in the end, the problem is that those pointers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 142.07999999999998,
          "en": "to arrays or objects in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "don't change if a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 146.763,
          "en": "inside of an array or object changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "So when Angular compares the old to the new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 155.763,
          "en": "it just sees the same pointer to the same array in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 161.52,
          "en": "So therefore, to get Angular to run transform again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "you must update your array in a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "here in onReset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 170.7,
          "en": "Instead of overriding one value in the array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "you need to override the array as a whole,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "which you could do by copying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "this historicTemperatures into a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 184.443,
          "en": "which we could store in a newTemps constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 189.66,
          "en": "And then you would reach out to this newTemps array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 193.77,
          "en": "so to that copy and replace the number there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.77,
          "end": 196.8,
          "en": "and then replace this historicTemperatures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.8,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "with this new array, so with that copied array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "With that, you got a brand new array in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "and a brand new reference, and therefore, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 211.07999999999998,
          "en": "if you reload and you click on one of these items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.07999999999998,
          "end": 213,
          "en": "you will now see it changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213,
          "end": 214.95,
          "en": "It then is also automatically moved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.95,
          "end": 219.42000000000002,
          "en": "because Angular does re-execute that transform method now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.42000000000002,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "and does sort that array again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "that's why Angular also automatically moves it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "Which in turn means that the indexes also get messed up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 232.17000000000002,
          "en": "because the indexes in the rendered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 236.1,
          "en": "are now not in line with the indexes in the input data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.1,
          "end": 237.81,
          "en": "But that's not too important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.81,
          "end": 241.23,
          "en": "because this lecture was about understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.23,
          "end": 244.86,
          "en": "how this behaves here and how you need to update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.86,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "array or object values to get this transform method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 252.873,
          "en": "to run again, though there also is an alternative to that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
